## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-Realtime-2
- **Short description:** OpenAI's most capable realtime voice model: speech-to-speech interactions with configurable reasoning effort, stronger instruction following, and more reliable tool use for complex voice-agent workflows. Successor to GPT-Realtime-1.5.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI API, Realtime endpoint only (`v1/realtime`). All other endpoints (Chat Completions, Responses, Live sessions, transcription/translation) not supported. Realtime WebSocket/WebRTC session API.
- **Release / knowledge:** release date not stated on the docs page (snapshots list only `gpt-realtime-2`); knowledge cutoff Sep 30, 2024.
- **IDs:** `openai/gpt-realtime-2` (no Free ID exists on Zen)
- **Context window:** 128,000 total tokens; 32,000 max output tokens (OpenAI model docs page, fetched 2026-09-27).
- **Modalities:** input text, audio, image; output text, audio; reasoning token support with configurable reasoning effort; tool calls yes (function_calling); prompt caching supported.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-27):** text $4.00 in / $24.00 out per 1M (cached input $0.40); audio $32.00 in / $64.00 out per 1M (cached input $0.40); image input $5.00 per 1M (cached $0.50). Paid only. Higher reasoning effort increases latency and token usage.
- **Architecture:** proprietary; realtime speech-to-speech reasoning model. Comparison from docs: GPT-Realtime-1.5 is $4/$16 text — Realtime-2 costs 50% more on text output.

